# Composable Agent Runtime PoC

Read `@AGENTS.md` in this folder. It is the authoritative context for this workspace:
package boundaries, execution realms, test topology, evidence policy, and CLI output
conventions. This rule exists so that context also reaches Inline Edit and Tab, which
do not read `AGENTS.md`.

## Scope

This folder is self-contained. When it is opened as the workspace root, Cursor does not
read `.cursor/rules` from the monorepo above it — and it should not: those rules govern
the shipping packages (SDK, native addons, registry) and their ticket, CI, and release
flow. Do not go looking for them.

## Always true here

- The PoC exists to prove package boundaries. A change that blurs one is a finding, not
  a detail — see `@AGENTS.md` "Package boundaries", and use the `boundary-review` skill.
- Every file belongs to an execution realm (Bun / Node / Bare / React Native). Check the
  realm before writing an import; see `@AGENTS.md` "Execution realms".
- Never delete, skip, or weaken an existing test to make a change pass.
- `bun run verify` is the gate before declaring a change done. Use the targeted
  `bun run test:<package>` while iterating.
